WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.010 --> 00:00:07.810
- There was this boy in my class

00:00:07.810 --> 00:00:09.280
when I was in fifth grade

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:12.610
who would walk into class
and do the Nazi salute.

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:14.840
He eventually got the rest of the class

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:16.120
to follow his lead

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:18.840
and they would start the mornings like so.

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:19.920
I told the teacher

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:22.760
that it made me upset, as I was Jewish.

00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:24.050
She laughed and told me

00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:26.783
she'd take care of it, she didn't.

00:00:29.458 --> 00:00:32.230
(soft music)

00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:34.220
- [Narrator] Dealing with
prejudice has long been a part

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:35.560
of the Jewish experience.

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:37.630
And with acts of antisemitism on the rise,

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:39.460
we partnered with YouTube Originals

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:40.660
and the SpringHill Company

00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:42.800
on our Recipe For Change series,

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:45.480
a one hour special featuring
three dinner conversations

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:47.520
about important social issues

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:50.320
and how we can engender positive change.

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:52.040
But we also wanted to hear from you.

00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:54.520
So we collected anonymously,
submitted secrets

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:56.840
from Jewish people about their experiences

00:00:56.840 --> 00:00:58.320
and we invited other Jewish people

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:00.150
to read about these secrets.

00:01:00.150 --> 00:01:03.460
In doing so, we strive to
create empathy and understanding

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:06.260
toward the challenges that
Jewish people face every day.

00:01:09.248 --> 00:01:11.680
(paper clacks)

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:13.920
- When my mom was a kid in the south

00:01:14.830 --> 00:01:17.700
she used to get spit on for being Jewish.

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:19.230
So when she had kids,

00:01:19.230 --> 00:01:22.640
she made the decision to not raise us

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:25.933
in the Jewish culture for our safety.

00:01:28.610 --> 00:01:29.803
- Can I say this word?

00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:33.580
My boyfriend called me
a (beep) to his friend

00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:34.740
and he thought it was okay

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:37.410
because his friend was Jewish too.

00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:41.220
This was the first time I
have ever been called that.

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:42.470
When I was in high school

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:46.170
my seat partner was drawing swastikas

00:01:46.170 --> 00:01:48.140
on his lunchbox.

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:50.590
And I asked him to stop.

00:01:50.590 --> 00:01:53.120
And our other seat partner was Jewish.

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:55.900
And he was like, "Oh my
grandma's a Holocaust survivor.

00:01:55.900 --> 00:01:57.390
She'll be fine with it.

00:01:57.390 --> 00:01:59.137
I'm fine with it, whatever."

00:02:00.590 --> 00:02:01.960
And that was kind of the first time

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:04.530
I encountered internalized Semitism.

00:02:04.530 --> 00:02:07.380
To be called that by
someone you're so close to

00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:10.490
is really harmful.

00:02:10.490 --> 00:02:13.770
I don't think I could come
back from something like that.

00:02:13.770 --> 00:02:16.170
- When I was at a friend's
house, when I was eight

00:02:16.170 --> 00:02:17.290
my friend's dad came in

00:02:17.290 --> 00:02:19.270
and poured holy water on my head

00:02:19.270 --> 00:02:21.670
and said, "Devil, be gone."

00:02:21.670 --> 00:02:23.950
It was one of many
experiences I had as a kid

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:27.543
that broke down my naive
ideal view of the world.

00:02:29.570 --> 00:02:31.700
I mean, I know it's your friend's dad,

00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:34.520
but I don't know how friendly that sounds.

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:35.880
I would say talk to your friend.

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:37.030
This is a direct situation

00:02:37.030 --> 00:02:38.820
where if that's a true friend of yours,

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:41.400
you could be like, "Hey man,
you need to talk to your dad."

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:43.940
Much like, I think we've all
been talking to our parents

00:02:43.940 --> 00:02:44.910
over the last couple years

00:02:44.910 --> 00:02:47.560
and kind of trying to
reteach them some concepts.

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:49.930
That's crazy, when he was eight years old,

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:51.163
that's completely awful.

00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:55.000
- There was this boy in my class

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:56.850
when I was in fifth grade

00:02:56.850 --> 00:02:58.230
who would walk into class

00:02:58.230 --> 00:03:00.380
and do the Nazi salute.

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:02.700
He eventually got the rest of the class

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:04.180
to follow his lead

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:06.990
and they would start the mornings like so.

00:03:06.990 --> 00:03:08.920
I told the teacher that it made me upset

00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:10.650
as I was Jewish.

00:03:10.650 --> 00:03:11.860
She laughed and told me

00:03:11.860 --> 00:03:15.270
she'd take care of it, she didn't.

00:03:15.270 --> 00:03:19.300
Around that time, I guess,
when I was in first grade too

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:22.840
I had a librarian read
a story to the class

00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:26.010
about The Christmas story

00:03:26.010 --> 00:03:27.600
but then she told the whole class

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:31.430
that Jews were responsible
for killing Jesus.

00:03:31.430 --> 00:03:35.500
And so then I had a classroom
full of first graders

00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:38.120
yelling at me, calling
me, "Christ killer."

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:41.650
And I came home crying to my mom

00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:44.123
that I didn't wanna be Jewish anymore,

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:46.493
at the age of seven.

00:03:47.591 --> 00:03:50.570
(paper clacks)

00:03:50.570 --> 00:03:53.220
- My safta is the only one in my family

00:03:53.220 --> 00:03:54.380
who is practicing.

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:58.910
And I am worried that if I
am ever out as trans to her

00:03:58.910 --> 00:04:00.373
she would not except me.

00:04:02.500 --> 00:04:07.260
Wow, that hits close.

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:09.840
I am transgender.

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:14.840
And my safta, she passed away.

00:04:15.050 --> 00:04:17.440
Though, I think she would've (sighs)

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:18.910
I don't know if she would've accepted me.

00:04:18.910 --> 00:04:22.530
And I have grandparents that accept me

00:04:22.530 --> 00:04:27.160
and for you to go through this, I'm sorry.

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:30.633
My own father doesn't accept
me for being transgender.

00:04:32.912 --> 00:04:34.729
And that's really hard.

00:04:34.729 --> 00:04:37.312
(paper clacks)

00:04:38.490 --> 00:04:41.350
- Too many people feel way too comfortable

00:04:41.350 --> 00:04:44.923
making casual Holocaust
jokes right to my face.

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:53.760
It's hard that we've completely normalized

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:56.810
making Holocaust jokes, antisemitic jokes.

00:04:56.810 --> 00:04:58.770
And I've heard it all before

00:04:58.770 --> 00:05:01.520
played off as, "I was just kidding.

00:05:01.520 --> 00:05:03.100
People do it all the time.

00:05:03.100 --> 00:05:04.540
Jewish comedians do it."

00:05:04.540 --> 00:05:08.110
But in reality, it hurts a lot,

00:05:08.110 --> 00:05:10.560
especially when you
start to internalize it.

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:12.060
And the minute we start

00:05:12.060 --> 00:05:14.410
to kind of get desensitized to it

00:05:14.410 --> 00:05:15.830
is when we allow people

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:18.403
to just kind of walk all over us.

00:05:19.290 --> 00:05:21.270
- I don't want to have kids

00:05:21.270 --> 00:05:22.580
but knowing that I exist

00:05:22.580 --> 00:05:24.680
because my ancestors survived

00:05:24.680 --> 00:05:27.030
1000s of years of persecution,

00:05:27.030 --> 00:05:29.930
because my grandparents
survived the Holocaust,

00:05:29.930 --> 00:05:32.363
means that I will have kids.

00:05:37.460 --> 00:05:41.500
That's an enormous amount of pressure

00:05:41.500 --> 00:05:44.860
for anyone to carry around

00:05:44.860 --> 00:05:47.360
but to carry around the weight

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:49.940
of all of that generational trauma

00:05:49.940 --> 00:05:52.890
and have it bleed into

00:05:52.890 --> 00:05:57.890
how your family looks and
what you want for your family,

00:06:00.001 --> 00:06:01.450
that's a lot.

00:06:01.450 --> 00:06:04.200
- I am a black convert to Judaism.

00:06:04.200 --> 00:06:06.930
Last Halloween, a white kid around my age

00:06:06.930 --> 00:06:09.490
was dressed up as a stereotypical

00:06:09.490 --> 00:06:12.150
and quite offensive Jewish caricature.

00:06:12.150 --> 00:06:13.280
I told him I was Jewish.

00:06:13.280 --> 00:06:17.270
And he said, and quote,
"You can't be a Jew,

00:06:17.270 --> 00:06:18.120
you're a (beep)."

00:06:19.160 --> 00:06:20.403
I never told anyone.

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:26.453
I'm half black and Jewish.

00:06:27.948 --> 00:06:32.948
And I've received the
same exact type of hate.

00:06:37.670 --> 00:06:40.220
- I was in the synagogue
during the Poway shooting.

00:06:41.340 --> 00:06:43.190
Thank God I wasn't personally wounded

00:06:44.210 --> 00:06:47.920
but I did witness death and
tragedy that fateful day.

00:06:47.920 --> 00:06:49.517
I found myself repeating,

00:06:49.517 --> 00:06:52.250
"I'd rather die firm in faith

00:06:53.500 --> 00:06:56.247
than live in fear without meaning."

00:06:57.150 --> 00:06:58.773
This was the Chabad of Poway.

00:06:59.730 --> 00:07:00.733
I know the rabbi.

00:07:01.990 --> 00:07:04.040
I know so many of his congregants.

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:05.263
It hit home.

00:07:06.640 --> 00:07:08.330
When you die firm in faith

00:07:08.330 --> 00:07:10.540
it means your whole life,

00:07:10.540 --> 00:07:13.100
you lived with a purpose.

00:07:13.100 --> 00:07:16.220
You lived being proud of who you are.

00:07:16.220 --> 00:07:17.670
- Sometimes I even get uncomfortable

00:07:17.670 --> 00:07:20.100
when I see other people
with Stars of David,

00:07:20.100 --> 00:07:22.200
because I fear for them.

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:26.230
I fear, "Is this person
going to experience

00:07:26.230 --> 00:07:28.010
some kind of interaction

00:07:28.010 --> 00:07:31.970
that's unwelcomed or mean or cruel

00:07:31.970 --> 00:07:34.387
for simply being who they are?"

00:07:36.450 --> 00:07:37.543
- This is real.

00:07:39.130 --> 00:07:41.163
This is real.

00:07:43.730 --> 00:07:48.263
Be strong, be firm, be happy.

